{"tool_name":"snt","contents":["neubias","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"snt","home":"https://imagej.net/SNT","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A Unifying Toolbox for Quantification of Neuronal Anatomy.\n\nThis repository hosts the scripts that were used to assemble the figures of the SNT publication.\n\nThe ImageJ framework for quantification of neuronal anatomy.\n\nThese scripts are intended to run from a Fiji installation subscribed to the Neuroanatomy update site, as detailed in the SNT documentation. Scripts relying on sciview/Cx3D functionality, also require the optional subscription to the SciView-Unstable update site. Since data is frequently downloaded from external servers, an internet connection is required.\n\nSNT is ImageJ's framework for semi-automated tracing, visualization, quantitative analyses and modeling of neuronal morphology.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:59:58Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-20T09:06:09Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:snt","credit":[{"email":"ferreirat@janelia.hhmi.org","name":"Tiago A. Ferreira","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"type":["Installation instructions"],"url":"https://imagej.net/SNT#Installation"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Neurite measurement","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3450"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"},{"term":"Splitting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3359"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"SNT","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.07.13.179325"}],"topic":[{"term":"Anatomy","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3067"},{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Neurobiology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3304"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"SNT","home":"https://bio.tools/snt","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A Unifying Toolbox for Quantification of Neuronal Anatomy.\n\nThis repository hosts the scripts that were used to assemble the figures of the SNT publication.\n\nThe ImageJ framework for quantification of neuronal anatomy.\n\nThese scripts are intended to run from a Fiji installation subscribed to the Neuroanatomy update site, as detailed in the SNT documentation. Scripts relying on sciview/Cx3D functionality, also require the optional subscription to the SciView-Unstable update site. Since data is frequently downloaded from external servers, an internet connection is required.\n\nSNT is ImageJ's framework for semi-automated tracing, visualization, quantitative analyses and modeling of neuronal morphology.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:snt/undefined/imagej.net","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1101/2020.07.13.179325","ref_count":0,"refs":[]}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://imagej.net/plugins/snt"},{"status":301,"url":"https://imagej.net/plugins/snt/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/snt","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://imagej.net/plugins/snt"},{"status":301,"url":"https://imagej.net/plugins/snt/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p><span>SNT is ImageJ\u2019s framework for tracing, visualization, quantitative analyses and modeling of neuronal morphology. For tracing, SNT supports modern multidimensional microscopy data, semi-automated and automated routines, and options for editing traces. For data analysis, SNT features advanced visualization tools, access to all major morphology databases, and support for whole-brain circuitry data.</span></p>","summary":"","value":"<p><span>SNT is ImageJ\u2019s framework for tracing, visualization, quantitative analyses and modeling of neuronal morphology. For tracing, SNT supports modern multidimensional microscopy data, semi-automated and automated routines, and options for editing traces. For data analysis, SNT features advanced visualization tools, access to all major morphology databases, and support for whole-brain circuitry data.</span></p>"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2025-10-27T02:14:00+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2025-10-27T00:49:57+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<h3>How do I cite SNT?</h3>  <p><strong>Note that neither the main <a href=\"/software/fiji#publication\">Fiji article</a>, nor the first <a href=\"#what-is-the-difference-between-snt-and-simple-neurite-tracer\">Simple Neurite Tracer</a> publication are appropriate citations for SNT. The proper citation for SNT is</strong>:</p>  <ul>   <li><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-021-01105-7\">doi:10.1038/s41592-021-01105-7</a></li> </ul>  <p>In addition, you should also cite any additional modules that you may use:</p>  <ul>   <li><strong><a href=\"/plugins/snt/sholl\">Sholl Analysis</a></strong> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/nmeth.3125\">doi:10.1038/nmeth.3125</a></li>   <li><strong><a href=\"/plugins/snt/modeling\">Cx3D</a></strong> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3389/neuro.10.025.2009\">doi:10.3389/neuro.10.025.2009</a></li>   <li><strong><a href=\"/plugins/snt/extending#tubular-geodesics\">Tubular Geodesics</a></strong> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1109/cvpr.2012.6247722\">doi:10.1109/cvpr.2012.6</a></li></ul>","value":"<h3>How do I cite SNT?</h3>  <p><strong>Note that neither the main <a href=\"/software/fiji#publication\">Fiji article</a>, nor the first <a href=\"#what-is-the-difference-between-snt-and-simple-neurite-tracer\">Simple Neurite Tracer</a> publication are appropriate citations for SNT. The proper citation for SNT is</strong>:</p>  <ul>   <li><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-021-01105-7\">doi:10.1038/s41592-021-01105-7</a></li> </ul>  <p>In addition, you should also cite any additional modules that you may use:</p>  <ul>   <li><strong><a href=\"/plugins/snt/sholl\">Sholl Analysis</a></strong> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/nmeth.3125\">doi:10.1038/nmeth.3125</a></li>   <li><strong><a href=\"/plugins/snt/modeling\">Cx3D</a></strong> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3389/neuro.10.025.2009\">doi:10.3389/neuro.10.025.2009</a></li>   <li><strong><a href=\"/plugins/snt/extending#tubular-geodesics\">Tubular Geodesics</a></strong> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1109/cvpr.2012.6247722\">doi:10.1109/cvpr.2012.6"}],"comments_2023":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1761529034,"last_comment_uid":4061,"status":2}],"free_tagging":[{"target_id":4212,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"13730f21-9367-4730-ba0e-a6dbfd2fdab5","url":"/taxonomy/term/4212"}],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1761529034,"last_comment_uid":4061,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Tiago Ferreira orcid.org/0000-0001-6866-1540"},{"value":"Cameron Arshadi orcid.org/0000-0002-1885-080X"},{"value":"Kyle Harrington orcid.org/0000-0002-7237-1973"}],"has_biological_terms":[{"target_id":4520,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"8690ed50-d23e-4d6d-97f0-2274